<content><![CDATA[<p>Check your understanding of this lesson. Your answers aren't recorded.</p>
<multiple-choice question="Why add support (holding) edges near a hard edge before subdividing?" single-option="" randomize="">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To keep the edge sharp when the mesh is smoothed" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To reduce the polygon count">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To create UV seams">
  <input type="checkbox" value="To make the object symmetrical">
</multiple-choice>
<true-false-question question="Modifiers such as Bevel, Mirror and Boolean let you change a model without permanently altering its base mesh.">
  <input type="checkbox" value="True" data-correct="true">
  <input type="checkbox" value="False">
</true-false-question>
<self-check title="Think it through">
  <p slot="question">When is a boolean operation a good choice, and what problems should you watch for?</p>
  <p>Booleans are quick for cutting holes and combining shapes, especially while blocking out. Watch for messy n-gons, shading artifacts and non-manifold geometry, and clean up the topology or keep the boolean as a non-destructive modifier.</p>
</self-check>
